WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Clutch and shift. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Explain torque interruption and ratio changes

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A clutch uses friction surfaces to connect engine torque to the gearbox. During engagement, slip converts some energy into heat.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: If the two sides rotate at different speeds, the clutch is still slipping; equal speed means it is locked in this simplified model.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Cause-and-effect sequence

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Explain torque interruption and ratio changes
